course: dictionary
lesson: 4003
title: Gap: space, difference, pause
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A gap is an empty space or opening between two things. It can also be a difference between two amounts, or a time when something stops. The words around a gap tell you which meaning is right. «A new paragraph is shown by an indent (a small gap at the start of the line).» Here the clue is «a small gap at the start of the line», so gap means an empty space.
explain: Look at «the clear gap just above the spout». Clear tells you the gap is empty, with nothing in it but air. The white cloud near the kettle is not the steam itself, so the gap is the space where you cannot see anything. Always ask: what is the empty part here?
explain: Gap can also mean a difference. «Tokyo's like a million hours ahead» is an exaggeration, because a million only means "a lot". The writer then says «in winter the real gap is 9 hours». The gap is the difference between two times, and you can work it out by counting.
explain: Gap can mean a part you have not learned yet, or a missing piece. «Stories grow because people fill gaps with guesses.» Here the gaps are the missing parts of a story, and people fill them in. If you have a gap in what you know, you can fill it by learning more.
fact: A gap is an empty space or opening between two things, such as a gap in a fence.
fact: A gap can be a difference between two amounts, such as the gap between two scores.
fact: A gap can be a time when something stops, such as «a gap of two weeks».
fact: A gap in what you know is a part you have not learned yet.
fact: To «fill the gap» means to put in what is missing; to «close the gap» means to make a difference smaller.
exercise: «A new paragraph is shown by an indent (a small gap at the start of the line).» What is the gap here? | A word that is missing from the story | *A small empty space at the start of the line | A big mistake in the book | A loud noise made by the printer
exercise: «In winter the real gap is 9 hours.» What does gap mean here? | *The difference between two times | A time when something stops | An empty hole in a wall | A part you have not learned yet
exercise: «Stories grow because people fill gaps with guesses.» What are the gaps in this sentence? | Differences between two scores | *Missing parts of a story | Long pauses in a film | Holes in a fence
test: In «a gap of two weeks», what does gap mean? | A difference between two amounts | An empty space between two things | A part you have not learned yet | *A time when something stops
test: In «the clear gap just above the spout», which word fits best in place of gap? | question | mistake | *space | noise
exam: Which sentence uses gap to mean a difference between two amounts? | *The gap between the two scores was only two points | I took a gap of two weeks off school | There is a gap in my knowledge of rivers | The fence has a gap at the bottom
